---

# 34. FINAL PRODUCT DEFINITION

The final MVP should feel like a credible technology service company with a marketplace-style browsing experience.

The desired experience is:

```text
SEARCHABLE
CLEAR
PROFESSIONAL
HUMAN
TECHNICAL
TRUSTWORTHY
FAST
```

The website should not feel like:

```text
GENERIC AI LANDING PAGE
FAKE MARKETPLACE
SHOPEE CLONE
OVER-DESIGNED CYBERPUNK UI
UNFINISHED TEMPLATE
```

---

# 35. FINAL USER FLOW

```text
USER VISITS WEBSITE
        ↓
SEARCHES A PROBLEM OR SERVICE
        ↓
FINDS A RELEVANT SERVICE
        ↓
READS SERVICE DETAILS
        ↓
UNDERSTANDS REQUIREMENTS AND RISKS
        ↓
CONTACTS WHATSAPP OR TELEGRAM CS
        ↓
HUMAN CONSULTATION
        ↓
SERVICE PROCESS AGREED
        ↓
REMOTE PREPARATION WHEN APPLICABLE
        ↓
EXECUTION CONTINUES OUTSIDE MVP WEBSITE
```

---

# END OF PRD

**Implementation principle:** Build the MVP as a polished, scalable frontend product. Do not pretend backend functionality exists. Optimize the real business workflow: discovery, understanding, trust, consultation, and remote preparation.
